OL,3,GNEWSACouncil debate for at-risk outdoor
OL,4,Acentre
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than 2,000 people have signed a
OL,7,Fpetition calling for the preservation
OL,8,Fof a much-loved outdoor education
OL,9,Fcentre, sparking a future council
OL,10,Fdebate.
OL,12,FNorth Tyneside Council has been urged
OL,13,Fto make a U-turn on its decision to
OL,14,Fclose  Cumbria-based High Borrans by
OL,15,FNovember.
OL,17,FThe Labour-led local authority has
OL,18,Fconfirmed the petition, which has
OL,19,Famassed 2,410 signatures, will be
OL,20,Fincluded in next month's full council
OL,21,Fmeeting.
OL,23,APub: 17-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
